## Overview

With `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FP8BMM=1` on gfx950, each DeepSeek-V4 attention layer allocated its own bf16 copy of the rotary cos/sin tables for the FP8 `wo_a` inverse RoPE. This PR builds one pair per rotary module, which `get_rope` already shares across layers, and has every layer read it. On DeepSeek-V4-Flash TP8 this frees 5.13 GiB per GPU, all of which goes to the KV cache.

