## Description

This PR adds an MXFP4 indexer path for DeepSeek-V4-Flash to the B200 sparse-attention decode operator introduced in #22223. `spec_dsa.op.run` scores the paged indexer keys, selects the exact top 512 compressed KV rows, and computes attention over those rows and the sliding window with the model’s attention sink. Callers use the operator directly. Model integration is a follow-up. [Review the 14 commits on top of #22223](https://github.com/longcheng-nv/TensorRT-LLM/compare/5027cc1123ef1c37c5fed2a5a59be01e04e9061c...1c425c82266f8e3b3716e3fdf64e181eb092cb46)

## Description

Per-rank `ShardedFp8MultiHeadEmbedding` share names include `tp_rank`. An off-home worker with an unclaimed share could wait two minutes before allocating its first table. A precise 120-second first-table stall was observed in the DSv4.1 startup investigation motivating this change.

This PR reduces the initial off-home claim grace from **120 seconds to 2 seconds**, preserving the existing behavior for:

- immediate joins to an existing owner, including descriptor/metadata pass-through;
- self-claim and allocation after the election grace;
- the per-process elapsed-time budget

## Description

`seed_prompt` loads a new request's prompt into the occurrence-penalty state (`PenaltyState.counts` / `prompt_mask`). That state is used by one-model speculative decoding (for example MTP) when `enable_penalty=True`. It runs on the executor thread once per newly admitted penalized request, from `prepare_inputs` inside `model_engine.forward`.

It synchronized with the device up to 4 times per call:

1. a blocking `prompt_tokens.to(device)`;
2. boolean-mask filtering of out-of-vocab ids;
3. `.numel()` on the filtered device tensors;
4. `torch.unique` for the ignored prefix.

